{title: Blessed Assurance}
{lyricist: Fanny J. Crosby}
{composer: Phoebe P. Knapp}
{year: 1873}
{key: D}
{time: 9/8}
{meta: tune ASSURANCE}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to ASSURANCE}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags assurance, testimony}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Blessed as[G]surance, [D]Jesus is mine!
O what a [E7]foretaste of [A]glory di[A7]vine!
[D]Heir of sal[G]vation, [D]purchase of [Bm]God,
[D]Born of His [A]Spirit, [A7]washed in His [D]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]This is my [G]story, [D]this is my song,
[D]Praising my [E7]Savior [A]all the day [A7]long;
[D]This is my [G]story, [D]this is my [Bm]song,
[D]Praising my [A]Savior [A7]all the day [D]long.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Perfect sub[G]mission, [D]perfect delight,
Visions of [E7]rapture now [A]burst on my [A7]sight;
[D]Angels de[G]scending [D]bring from a[Bm]bove
[D]Echoes of [A]mercy, [A7]whispers of [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Perfect sub[G]mission, [D]all is at rest;
I in my [E7]Savior am [A]happy and [A7]blest,
[D]Watching and [G]waiting, [D]looking a[Bm]bove,
[D]Filled with His [A]goodness, [A7]lost in His [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
